    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "QMqAH",
      "x": 1300,
      "y": 1560,
      "name": "DOC 01 People",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 400,
      "content": "01 PEOPLE — the directory is the chat list\n\nWHAT IT IS — Every employee, in one column: name, role, a live status dot, and one line saying what they are doing right now (not their last message). Selecting anyone opens the thread. The right panel is that person's profile, folded in from the deleted profile screen: what they are on now, what they may do alone versus what needs your word, what they have spent against their ceiling, and the files they made lately. Hiring is the last row of the directory — it opens the new person's thread, so the first session starts as a conversation.\n\nFOLDS IN — the old chats sidebar, per-employee DMs, the agent profile screen, the staff list, the group channels, and the start-a-session modal.\n\nDROPPED — the NEEDS YOU pin. Attention lives in the inbox stack only; that pin was the same queue projected a third time. Goal channels are gone too: a goal is a node on the board, and talk about it happens in the thread of whoever owns it.\n\nNEEDS — who exists, their role and presence, what each is currently working on and its cost so far, unread counts per thread, the per-person authority summary (three lines is enough — the full list is surface 04), the month's spend against that person's ceiling, and recent output as file paths.\n\nWRITES — send a message; hire someone; pause a person; revise their role. Approval cards can be acted on inline here: same governed action as the inbox, in the place the work was discussed.\n\nGUARDRAIL — a directory of colleagues, not a fleet console. No grid of agent tiles, no batch operations, no prompt or skill editors on this surface."
    },
