    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "HvOxd",
      "x": 4500,
      "y": 1560,
      "name": "DOC 03 Inbox",
      "width": 1440,
      "height": 400,
      "content": "03 INBOX — a stack, reviewed one card at a time\n\nWHAT IT IS — Everything waiting on your word, ordered by what blocks the most work, presented as a deck: the top card is the whole item — who raised it, what it will do, the exact text or amount, and why it needed you at all — with the action in place and keyboard review (approve / decline / skip). Behind it, the rest of the stack is visible as depth, and the next three are listed underneath so the queue is never a mystery. Updates that need no decision are counted, not stacked.\n\nWHY A STACK — a list with a detail pane invites triage-by-scanning; a stack asks for a decision on one thing and then hands you the next. The count and the sort are stated on the surface so the order is never a guess.\n\nFOLDS IN — the sidebar needs-you pin, the board's waiting-on-you column, the per-thread approval cards, and the update events that previously had no home.\n\nNEEDS — the merged set of decisions, outside-effect approvals, escalations and payment confirmations; for each one the actor, the artifact or amount, the waiting time, the task and goal it belongs to, and the authority setting that made it require you. Read state is a watermark, not a per-row flag.\n\nWRITES — approve (held, not clicked); decline; open the draft; ask the person a question, which posts into their thread.\n\nGUARDRAIL — a projection, never a store. Every card deep-links to its source; dismissing changes nothing about the record; the reason line always names the standing setting on surface 04 that put it here, so the queue explains itself and can be shortened at the source."
    },
